  "rationale": "With no defences the attack succeeds: phish_workstation gives a foothold and stolen_user. pivot_internal then gives reach_internal, because segmentation is not deployed. From there the chain runs auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So at least one control is needed. Both exfiltration paths (db and fileserver) need stolen_dbadmin, and only dump_dbadmin_dc provides it, which requires admin_dc. admin_dc requires foothold_dc, and auth_dc is the only technique that grants foothold_dc. auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks foothold_dc, then admin_dc, then stolen_dbadmin, so exfiltration is impossible. Minimum = 1."
